---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';

// Pricing benchmark report terms (offers/pricing-benchmark/decisions/site_copy.md D).
// Payment: PayPal invoice, as in site_copy.md D clause 9 (owner decision of
// 6 October 2026: PayPal until Payoneer is set up; DECISIONS.md decision 6). The
// 5 October wire wording is withdrawn. This text still departs from site_copy.md D
// in two places, and site_copy.md D needs the same edits before it is the single
// source again: clause 1 (delivery counted from the day the payment completes,
// because the buyer may pay days after the invoice is sent; clause 10 points to
// clause 1 for the delivery date) and clause 4 (re-read prices go through the same
// second check as routine re-checks, DECISIONS.md decision 6). Seller line: clause 1
// gets one line naming the seller only after the Ministry of Finance registration
// and the Saudi lawyer's written answer (DECISIONS.md decision 6); until then the
// terms name no seller. DEPLOY: set lastUpdated to the deploy date (en-US) in the
// deploy commit; it holds the date the text was written until then.
const lastUpdated = 'October 6, 2026';

const breadcrumbs = [
  { name: 'Home', url: '/' },
  { name: 'Pricing benchmark report terms', url: '/report-terms/' },
];
---

<Layout
  title="Pricing benchmark report terms | WrenchStack"
  description="The terms for WrenchStack pricing benchmark reports sold to software vendors: what you buy, sources and dates, independence, public listing of the sale, use, refunds and liability."
  breadcrumbs={breadcrumbs}
>
  <article class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-12">
    <header class="mb-8">
      <p class="mb-3 text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-orange-600">Legal</p>
      <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-slate-900 sm:text-4xl">Pricing benchmark report terms</h1>
      <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-slate-500">Last updated: {lastUpdated}</p>
    </header>

    <section class="prose prose-slate max-w-none">
      <p>
        These terms apply to every WrenchStack pricing benchmark report. They apply together with our
        <a href="/terms/">Terms of Use</a>; where the two differ, these terms apply.
      </p>

      <h2>1. What you buy</h2>
      <p>
        One report on one WrenchStack trade page, in English, emailed as a PDF to the address on the invoice by
        the delivery date. The delivery date falls the number of business days stated on the invoice after the day
        your payment completes. The report covers the platforms on that trade page on the day it
        is written, and places your product's published price, packaging and pricing terms against them.
        Questions go by email to <a href="mailto:bilal@wrenchstack.com">bilal@wrenchstack.com</a>; there are no
        calls or meetings.
      </p>

      <h2>2. Sources</h2>
      <p>
        The report uses vendors' public pages and what WrenchStack already publishes. Information another vendor
        sent us privately is not included unless it already appears on that vendor's WrenchStack listing. Each
        published price is read from the vendor's own page while the report is written, where that page can be
        read. Where it cannot, the report says so and shows the page used and the date it was last read.
      </p>

      <h2>3. Dates</h2>
      <p>
        Each figure is as read on the date it shows. Prices and terms change, and the report is not updated after
        delivery.
      </p>

      <h2>4. Independence</h2>
      <p>
        Whether you bought a report is not an input to any WrenchStack listing, Fit Score, ranking, award or
        reputation flag, or to whether a product is listed. Buying a report gives no preview of what we publish,
        no advance notice of changes and no say over what we publish. The report does not explain or recalculate
        any Fit Score and does not say how any vendor could change its position. Whether a product publishes a
        price is one of the three Fit Score factors (pricing transparency, 20%, set out on our
        <a href="/methodology/">methodology page</a>); the report describes published pricing for every platform,
        yours included, and computes no score. Prices we re-read for a report go through the same second check of
        the vendor's page as routine re-checks and are updated on WrenchStack for every platform on that trade
        page, buyer or not, no later than the day the report is delivered.
      </p>
      <p>
        We do not quote a price, send an invoice or take an order while an evaluation, correction, pricing
        question, dispute or reputation-flag review is open between your company and us, or within 30 days after
        the latest listing verdict, correction or reputation-flag email we sent you. If one of these opens after
        you have paid, it follows our normal process and timeline, your order continues, and the report ledger
        notes it and its outcome. A claim that a report sale affected a listing goes to
        <a href="mailto:hello@wrenchstack.com">hello@wrenchstack.com</a> with the page URL; each one gets a written
        reply, and a confirmed problem is corrected on the page and noted in the report ledger.
      </p>

      <h2>5. Public listing of the sale</h2>
      <p>
        We list each sale in the report ledger on
        <a href="/methodology/#report-ledger">wrenchstack.com/methodology/</a>: your company and product, the
        trade, the month of payment, the price paid, the order status, and your product's Fit Score, rank, award
        and reputation flag on that trade page when you ordered and today, with the cause of any difference. The
        figures from when you ordered are also stated on your invoice. The sale is also noted on your product's
        tool page and counted on the trade pages that list your product. Refunded orders stay listed. The
        report's cover states that your company paid for it and did not review or approve its contents.
      </p>

      <h2>6. Use</h2>
      <p>
        The report is for internal use by your company and its advisers. Without our written permission, do not
        publish it, resell it, share it outside your company, or quote it in advertising, sales material or
        comparisons with named competitors, and do not present it as a WrenchStack endorsement, ranking or award.
      </p>

      <h2>7. No warranty</h2>
      <p>
        The report is information, not legal, financial or pricing advice. It is provided as is, without any
        warranty of accuracy or completeness and without a guarantee of any result.
      </p>

      <h2>8. Corrections</h2>
      <p>
        If a figure differed from its source on the date shown, tell us by email within 30 days of delivery, with
        the source. If we confirm the error, we send a corrected PDF and make the same correction on the site.
      </p>

      <h2>9. Payment</h2>
      <p>
        Payment is by PayPal invoice in US dollars, due on receipt. Work starts when the payment completes. We add
        no fee.
      </p>

      <h2>10. Cancellation and refunds</h2>
      <p>
        You can cancel for a full refund at any time before delivery, and also if we have not delivered by the
        delivery date in clause 1. After delivery there is no refund, unless the report covers a
        different trade from the one ordered. A refund is not given because of anything WrenchStack publishes on
        its site.
      </p>

      <h2>11. Liability</h2>
      <p>
        Our total liability for a report is limited to the amount you paid for it. We are not liable for indirect
        or consequential loss or for lost profit. Nothing in these terms limits liability that the law does not
        allow to be limited.
      </p>

      <h2>12. Changes</h2>
      <p>
        We may change these terms. The version in force on the date of your invoice applies to your order.
      </p>
    </section>
  </article>
</Layout>
